WEBVTT

00:02.369 --> 00:05.270
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.506 --> 00:09.068
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.177 --> 00:12.442
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.547 --> 00:15.346
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.785 --> 00:18.913
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.021 --> 00:22.013
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.258 --> 00:23.920
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.027 --> 00:25.619
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.763 --> 00:30.497
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:36.241 --> 00:39.211
Hi, it's me, Peter, your TV cartoon pal.

00:39.378 --> 00:40.709
You know, Lois has been bitching lately

00:40.813 --> 00:43.213
that I watch too much TV
and don't read enough books,

00:43.315 --> 00:45.476
so I went to the library
and picked up three books

00:45.584 --> 00:50.022
by the greatest author
of the last thousand years, Stephen King.

00:50.123 --> 00:52.148
And tonight I'd like
to share them with you.

00:52.259 --> 00:55.024
<i>We begin with a little tale
called Stand by Me,</i>

00:55.129 --> 00:57.757
about four young boys
who went looking for a dead body

00:57.865 --> 01:00.163
and instead found themselves

01:01.102 --> 01:02.593
and also a dead body.

01:05.974 --> 01:08.442
<i>The year was 1955,</i>

01:08.544 --> 01:11.343
<i>and the voice in my head was
that of Richard Dreyfuss.</i>

01:11.447 --> 01:14.439
<i>I never had friends
like the ones I had when I was 12.</i>

01:14.551 --> 01:16.314
<i>There was me, Petey Lachance.</i>

01:16.419 --> 01:19.218
Anyone else fed up
with this over-saturation of media?

01:19.323 --> 01:21.416
Three channels and still nothing on.

01:21.525 --> 01:25.291
<i>Then there was Joey Duchamp.
The voice in his head was Roy Scheider.</i>

01:25.396 --> 01:27.024
<i>How are you, Richard?
Fine, Roy.</i>

01:27.132 --> 01:28.793
<i>- How are you?
Good, good.</i>

01:28.900 --> 01:31.232
<i>We should grab a drink
sometime and catch up.</i>

01:31.336 --> 01:33.463
<i>- Maybe reminisce about Jaws.
Great.</i>

01:33.572 --> 01:36.872
<i>You should give me a call sometime.
My number is 555...</i>

01:36.976 --> 01:40.434
<i>Wait, wait. What? 555?
- Yeah.</i>

01:40.546 --> 01:41.570
<i>You know what, Richard?</i>

01:41.681 --> 01:43.547
<i>If you don't want to have drinks,
just say so.</i>

01:43.650 --> 01:44.878
<i>You don't have to be a dick about it.</i>

01:44.985 --> 01:47.681
Oh, please! Make the voices stop!

01:47.821 --> 01:51.656
<i>And then there was Quag
Chambers. He was the leader of our gang.</i>

01:51.759 --> 01:53.124
<i>He had sex when he was five</i>

01:53.228 --> 01:55.458
<i>and committed his first rape
when he was 10,</i>

01:55.563 --> 01:57.827
<i>rape, of course, being legal in the '50s.</i>

01:57.932 --> 02:02.461
Beat those cards, fellas.
Giggity Giggity '50s Giggity.

02:02.571 --> 02:03.629
Hey, you guys.

02:03.739 --> 02:07.198
<i>Finally, there was Cleve Brown,
my pudgy black friend.</i>

02:07.310 --> 02:10.370
<i>I can still see him now,
all pudgy and black.</i>

02:10.547 --> 02:12.538
<i>Cleve, please.
We're busy looking at Playboy.</i>

02:12.649 --> 02:14.845
Look at the way
these women starve themselves.

02:14.952 --> 02:17.079
This one can't be more than 180 pounds.

02:17.188 --> 02:19.315
<i>This is way better than Playboy.</i>

02:19.423 --> 02:21.482
Do you guys want to see a dead body?

02:21.592 --> 02:23.254
Cleve, it's 1955.

02:23.362 --> 02:27.059
Please re-enter the clubhouse in
a more stereotypically animated fashion.

02:28.800 --> 02:31.964
Lord almighty! I done seen me
a dead body down by the lake.

02:32.071 --> 02:35.438
Sho' 'nough, I thought I'd go deef
and dumb when I saw me that dead body.

02:35.541 --> 02:37.532
Cleve, calm down.
You're not making any sense.

02:37.644 --> 02:41.012
<i>Every day it's a-getting closer...</i>

02:41.815 --> 02:44.340
<i>Anything was possible
as we set out that day,</i>

02:44.451 --> 02:46.043
<i>except contracting AIDS</i>

02:46.153 --> 02:48.782
<i>because AIDS had not yet
been invented by the government</i>

02:48.890 --> 02:51.882
<i>in an effort to eradicate
the homosexual community.</i>

02:51.993 --> 02:57.330
<i>Have gun, will travel
reads the card of a man</i>

02:57.433 --> 03:02.370
<i>A knight without armor in a savage land</i>

03:02.472 --> 03:03.734
Okay, I got another one.

03:03.840 --> 03:05.740
<i>Show me that smile again</i>

03:05.842 --> 03:07.742
<i>Show me that smile</i>

03:07.844 --> 03:11.906
<i>Don't waste another minute on your crying</i>

03:12.383 --> 03:15.352
<i>We decided to cut through
Old Man Pressman's junkyard,</i>

03:15.453 --> 03:18.719
<i>even though legend had it
that any kid caught scaling the fence</i>

03:18.824 --> 03:22.021
<i>ran the risk of being attacked
by the old man's dog,</i>

03:22.127 --> 03:26.086
<i>who would charge to the cry of
'"Chopper, sic balls. '"</i>

03:26.198 --> 03:28.258
I got a bad feeling about this.

03:28.368 --> 03:30.427
Hey! What are you kids doing?

03:30.537 --> 03:31.765
Oh, no! It's him!

03:31.871 --> 03:34.807
That's right. I'm Old Man Pressman.
I own the junkyard.

03:34.909 --> 03:37.173
I'm cranky 'cause all my stuff is junk.

03:37.278 --> 03:39.906
Why can't I have nice things?

03:40.014 --> 03:41.675
Chopper, sic them. Sic them, boy!

03:47.489 --> 03:49.252
<i>Now, he said, '"Sic them, boy. '"</i>

03:49.358 --> 03:50.587
<i>But what I heard was,</i>

03:50.693 --> 03:53.594
<i>'"Chopper, talk to disfigured
World War II veterans</i>

03:53.696 --> 03:55.721
<i>'"who aren't as bitter as they should be. '"</i>

03:55.832 --> 03:57.663
Glad I could do my part.

03:57.767 --> 03:59.395
I think you may have done too much.

04:00.170 --> 04:03.503
<i>Hey, how about this
brand new thing called rock and roll?</i>

04:03.607 --> 04:06.668
<i>Even though it was just invented,
we already remember it fondly.</i>

04:06.778 --> 04:09.269
<i>Here's Little Richard with Piano Riff Woo.</i>

04:11.249 --> 04:12.409
<i>Woo!</i>

04:14.119 --> 04:15.087
<i>Woo!</i>

04:16.822 --> 04:17.789
<i>Woo!</i>

04:19.725 --> 04:20.692
<i>Woo!</i>

04:21.427 --> 04:22.394
<i>Woo!</i>

04:22.863 --> 04:23.830
<i>Woo!</i>

04:25.098 --> 04:26.087
<i>Woo!</i>

04:29.449 --> 04:30.747
Fuck that.

04:31.319 --> 04:33.810
Man, this trip is dangerous.
Couldn't we have just taken a bus?

04:33.922 --> 04:37.153
No... black guy.

04:39.361 --> 04:42.091
Guys? Anyone know
when the next train is scheduled?

04:42.198 --> 04:45.224
Don't worry. If a train comes,
I'll warn you in slow motion.

04:51.708 --> 04:55.440
Train!

05:08.794 --> 05:10.261
My legs!

05:10.897 --> 05:14.594
Another train!

05:16.903 --> 05:20.670
What an odd, clustered train schedule!

05:21.041 --> 05:24.204
- Hey, sorry you got paralyzed, Joey.
- That's all right.

05:24.311 --> 05:27.076
Thanks for going all the way back
to the junkyard to get me this wheelchair.

05:27.182 --> 05:29.082
Boy, was Old Man Pressman angry.

05:31.753 --> 05:33.084
<i>We talked into the night,</i>

05:33.188 --> 05:36.647
<i>the kind of talk that seemed important
until you discover girls.</i>

05:36.759 --> 05:40.422
This House Un-American
Activities Committee is a travesty.

05:40.529 --> 05:44.557
And if we go into French Indochina,
it'll take us 30 years to get out.

05:44.668 --> 05:46.329
Levittown-type housing communities

05:46.436 --> 05:49.166
will replace individualism
with fear and conformity.

05:49.273 --> 05:52.402
What do you think of that new kid
at school, Marty McFly?

05:52.510 --> 05:55.240
Seems like he just showed up
out of nowhere.

05:59.151 --> 06:01.119
Well, there it is.

06:01.220 --> 06:02.744
<i>None of us could breathe.</i>

06:02.855 --> 06:05.551
<i>The twisted and mangled body
we had come to see</i>

06:05.658 --> 06:09.720
<i>was far more disgusting
than any of us could ever have imagined.</i>

06:10.130 --> 06:11.097
He's nasty.

06:12.923 --> 06:16.485
Out of my way, you little pip-squeaks.
I'm taking credit for finding this body.

06:17.662 --> 06:21.689
<i>It was the meanest guy
in town, Ace, and his whole gang,</i>

06:21.799 --> 06:25.736
<i>Beast Man, Mer-Man and,
for some reason, Norm from Cheers.</i>

06:25.838 --> 06:28.033
Hey, gang.
What, are we beating somebody up?

06:28.140 --> 06:31.269
Now, get lost. We'll take it from here.

06:34.714 --> 06:38.811
Kiss my grits, you cheap dime-store hood.

06:38.919 --> 06:41.012
This ain't over, Lachance.

06:41.122 --> 06:42.612
I mean, you have a gun right now.

06:42.723 --> 06:46.284
But tomorrow I'll get a gun
and come to your house and kill you.

06:46.394 --> 06:49.455
Oh. Yeah, I guess you could do that, huh?

06:49.564 --> 06:51.031
I mean, we live in the same town.

06:51.133 --> 06:54.034
And I can't just be on my guard
for the rest of my life.

06:54.136 --> 06:57.072
Boy, that is a major hole in this story.
Okay, take the body.

07:00.109 --> 07:02.339
<i>We never forgot
that wonderful summer.</i>

07:02.445 --> 07:05.006
<i>And eventually we all went
our separate ways.</i>

07:05.115 --> 07:07.515
<i>Joey learned to live
without the use of his legs</i>

07:07.618 --> 07:11.111
<i>and even went on to create
a wheelchair-type rugby game</i>

07:11.222 --> 07:14.282
<i>called Don't Feel Sorry For Us Ball.</i>

07:14.392 --> 07:17.759
<i>Cleve grew up
and went on to marry Rebecca Romijn.</i>

07:17.862 --> 07:19.660
<i>Actually, I'm not even joking about that.</i>

07:19.765 --> 07:23.826
<i>The fat kid from Stand by Me
is now married to Rebecca Romijn.</i>

07:23.936 --> 07:25.096
<i>Can you believe that?</i>

07:25.204 --> 07:27.503
<i>I swear to God. Look it up on the Internet.</i>

07:27.607 --> 07:29.336
<i>Doesn't that piss you off?</i>

07:29.443 --> 07:32.412
<i>Quag grew up to become
a famous Hollywood actor.</i>

07:32.512 --> 07:34.480
<i>Unfortunately, about a week ago,</i>

07:34.581 --> 07:38.040
<i>he took an overdose of designer drugs
at The Viper Room.</i>

07:38.152 --> 07:40.746
<i>He died on the curb outside,</i>

07:40.855 --> 07:45.088
<i>and now we're left with a harelipped
reminder of what might have been.</i>

07:50.132 --> 07:52.397
Hi. Welcome back from commercials.

07:52.502 --> 07:56.529
Joaquin Phoenix, if you're still watching,
you are a good sport and a trouper,

07:56.639 --> 07:59.939
and you passed our test,
and you can be our friend.

08:00.044 --> 08:03.343
And now for a segment we like
a little less than the first and the last.

08:03.447 --> 08:04.846
<i>Here's Misery.</i>

08:10.889 --> 08:11.856
Marcia, I've done it.

08:11.957 --> 08:14.152
I've finished the book,
and Snuggly Jeff is dead.

08:14.259 --> 08:15.693
And the readers are just gonna love it.

08:15.795 --> 08:17.854
Paul, I still wish I could talk you out of this.

08:17.964 --> 08:21.229
<i>Snuggly Jeffis the most successful
children's book series ever.</i>

08:21.334 --> 08:23.769
Yeah, but I want to get
into writing more serious stuff.

08:23.871 --> 08:25.168
You know, something
where the reader doesn't have

08:25.272 --> 08:27.035
a load in his pants while he's looking at it.

08:27.141 --> 08:29.132
Well, we'll talk about it
when you get back.

08:34.682 --> 08:35.649
<i>This just in.</i>

08:35.750 --> 08:39.187
<i>The Weather Service has reported
a big snowstorm on its way.</i>

08:41.924 --> 08:43.687
Oh, my God! Stephen King!

08:47.397 --> 08:49.422
Hey, this would make a neat story.

08:51.401 --> 08:52.368
Done.

09:12.190 --> 09:13.487
<i>I'm your number-one fan.</i>

09:13.825 --> 09:17.158
I'm your number-one fan.
I'm your number-one fan.

09:19.264 --> 09:21.755
Who... Who are you?

09:21.867 --> 09:24.028
I'm Stewie Wilkes. I saved your life.

09:24.136 --> 09:27.698
You were in a terrible car accident,
and you broke both your legs.

09:27.974 --> 09:28.941
I taste lipstick.

09:29.042 --> 09:31.306
- Am I wearing lipstick?
- Not anymore.

09:31.578 --> 09:34.844
You know, I am a huge Snuggly Jeff fan.
I've read all the books.

09:34.949 --> 09:36.644
Great. Hey, can you hand me
my cell phone?

09:36.751 --> 09:39.151
I gotta call my agent.
She's probably worried sick about me.

09:39.253 --> 09:41.118
It was destroyed in the accident.

09:41.222 --> 09:42.918
- Well, can I use yours?
- No reception up here.

09:43.024 --> 09:44.048
- Regular phone?
- Lines are down.

09:44.159 --> 09:45.126
- Pay phone?
- Road's closed.

09:45.227 --> 09:46.194
- E-mail?
- Dial-up.

09:46.294 --> 09:47.283
- Fax?
- Paper jam.

09:47.395 --> 09:48.362
- Morse code?
- Obsolete.

09:48.463 --> 09:49.862
Brain-damaged bicycle courier?

09:49.965 --> 09:53.163
I'm not quite so sure I can find my way.

09:56.038 --> 09:58.029
Yeah, you're gonna be here a while.

10:01.745 --> 10:04.305
Paul, quick question,
and feel free to say no,

10:04.414 --> 10:08.215
but I couldn't help but notice the new
Snuggly Jeff manuscript in your bag.

10:08.319 --> 10:11.345
And I was wondering if I could read it,
then kill you if I hate it?

10:11.456 --> 10:12.889
Well, I guess that'd be okay.

10:12.991 --> 10:14.219
Thank you, thank you, thank you!

10:14.325 --> 10:16.851
Can I read it while I touch your ear
and suck my thumb?

10:16.962 --> 10:18.793
- I guess.
- Goody, goody!

10:31.379 --> 10:33.904
Mmm. Mmm.

10:42.455 --> 10:46.756
- Stewie?
- I just finished the book, you dirty birdie.

10:46.860 --> 10:49.226
How could you? He can't be dead.

10:49.329 --> 10:51.593
Snuggly Jeff cannot be dead!

10:53.100 --> 10:55.831
Look, Stewie.
I've gone as far as I can with Snuggly Jeff,

10:55.937 --> 10:57.962
and I want to write
something more serious.

10:58.539 --> 11:01.838
Well, you are gonna write Snuggly Jeff
back to life, Mr. Man.

11:01.943 --> 11:03.844
Look, Stewie, first of all, you're insane,

11:03.946 --> 11:06.414
and second of all,
I have to be inspired before I write.

11:06.515 --> 11:08.449
Well, how about a little TV?

11:08.984 --> 11:11.715
<i>We now return
to Magnum, b. m.</i>

11:11.821 --> 11:14.984
<i>Magnum, I found a fingerprint smudge
at the crime scene.</i>

11:15.091 --> 11:16.854
<i>Do you have poo on your hands?</i>

11:18.061 --> 11:19.086
<i>A little.</i>

11:25.236 --> 11:27.671
No, no, no. This won't do, Paul.

11:27.772 --> 11:28.966
You can't just have Snuggly Jeff

11:29.074 --> 11:31.702
magically brought back to life
by a child's wish.

11:31.810 --> 11:33.141
It's insulting to the reader.

11:33.245 --> 11:35.612
- What do you mean?
- Well, it's just bad storytelling.

11:35.715 --> 11:37.182
Let's see. How can I explain this to you?

11:37.283 --> 11:39.274
<i>- Did you ever see the movie Contact?
- Yeah.</i>

11:39.385 --> 11:43.083
So, like, they spent a trillion dollars
building this mile-high space machine,

11:43.190 --> 11:44.714
and Jake Busey blows it up.

11:44.825 --> 11:47.919
So now they're all like,
"Oh, no! We can't use the space machine. "

11:48.028 --> 11:50.622
But then this other guy's like,
"Hey, it just so happens

11:50.731 --> 11:53.565
"I built another identical
trillion-dollar space machine

11:53.668 --> 11:55.932
"at my own expense
on the other side of the world. "

11:56.037 --> 11:58.505
And we're supposed to believe
no one noticed that?

11:58.606 --> 12:01.474
Well, I stood up in the theater,
and I said, "No!

12:01.577 --> 12:03.841
"You can't go into space
because the machine

12:03.946 --> 12:07.713
"already got blown up
by Jake-cockadoody-Busey. "

12:07.851 --> 12:09.478
- Start over!
- Fine.

12:09.586 --> 12:12.419
But you're gonna have to go into town
and get me some more paper. I'm all out.

12:12.522 --> 12:15.549
I don't know, Paul. Let me see
if I can get the Big Wheel started.

12:18.763 --> 12:20.754
I don't know, Paul. It's not starting.

12:22.133 --> 12:23.692
I'm afraid I'm gonna flood it.

12:26.905 --> 12:29.738
Okay, I got it now. I'll see you in a bit.

13:06.250 --> 13:07.979
He's too big for that car.

13:17.028 --> 13:18.017
Mr. Sheldon?

13:18.129 --> 13:19.620
Oh, my God! I'm saved!

13:19.732 --> 13:21.700
Let's get out of here
before Stewie gets back.

13:24.937 --> 13:26.234
My legs!

13:26.338 --> 13:29.797
Now I'm gonna have to spend
the rest of my life in a wheelchair.

13:29.909 --> 13:31.399
No, you're not.

13:36.584 --> 13:38.677
Well, that's it, Stewie. The book is done.

13:38.786 --> 13:41.983
- Can I go now?
- Oh, no, Paul. I'm not stupid.

13:42.089 --> 13:44.251
If I let you go,
you'll just run straight to the police

13:44.359 --> 13:46.122
and tell them I kidnapped you
and held you hostage

13:46.228 --> 13:47.695
and fondled you while you were asleep.

13:47.796 --> 13:48.956
No, I... Wait. What?

13:49.064 --> 13:50.463
You'll tell them
that while you were sleeping

13:50.565 --> 13:52.295
I did things to you
that you don't remember.

13:52.402 --> 13:55.394
- You fondled me while I was asleep?
- Yeah.

13:55.505 --> 13:57.530
- I don't think I like that.
- Well, it's done.

14:05.449 --> 14:08.044
Everybody still awake? All right, big finish.

14:08.153 --> 14:09.552
Now, you remember
that Stephen King story

14:09.654 --> 14:11.212
when the guy went up to the empty hotel?

14:11.323 --> 14:12.449
And there were those creepy twins?

14:12.557 --> 14:14.081
And the guy was running around
with that ax?

14:14.192 --> 14:15.353
And the kid talked to his finger?

14:15.461 --> 14:17.725
Can't you see Stewie doing that?

14:17.830 --> 14:19.991
<i>Well, here's The Shawshank Redemption.</i>

14:37.785 --> 14:42.519
<i>The first time I laid eyes on
Andy Dufresne, I didn't think much of him.</i>

14:42.624 --> 14:44.558
<i>He was a fat drink of water,</i>

14:44.660 --> 14:47.425
<i>the kind of drink of water that you know
your friend got from the bathroom</i>

14:47.530 --> 14:48.519
<i>and not from the kitchen.</i>

14:50.370 --> 14:53.669
Five packs of cigarettes says
the fat one breaks first tonight.

14:53.774 --> 14:56.335
You're on.
I'll take the Don Martin-looking one.

15:00.381 --> 15:03.351
Welcome to Shawshank Prison.
I'll be your warden.

15:03.452 --> 15:06.319
And even though I'm the only character
in this movie who's not a criminal,

15:06.422 --> 15:07.855
I will be the bad guy.

15:08.023 --> 15:10.856
Tomorrow's lunch is American chop suey,

15:10.961 --> 15:13.589
so you came here on a good day.
Good lunch.

15:14.564 --> 15:16.088
Look at those smiles.

15:27.613 --> 15:29.376
All right, lights out, ladies.

15:30.616 --> 15:34.052
It's funny because we are not ladies,
we are men.

15:34.152 --> 15:35.120
Shut up.

15:38.552 --> 15:41.988
<i>A month went by before
Andy said two words to somebody.</i>

15:42.089 --> 15:44.786
<i>As it turned out, that somebody was me.</i>

15:44.892 --> 15:46.120
Vagina boob.

15:46.928 --> 15:50.159
<i>Later, Andy came back
with more than two words.</i>

15:50.265 --> 15:52.734
I understand you're a man
who knows how to get things.

15:52.835 --> 15:56.134
I've been known to procure
various and sundry items.

15:56.238 --> 15:59.766
I don't understand what you just said.
I need stuff. Can you get it?

15:59.876 --> 16:01.844
- What do you need?
- I need a rock hammer.

16:01.945 --> 16:05.278
<i>- What's it for?
- I carve Star Wars figurines out of stone,</i>

16:05.382 --> 16:07.647
but it's also for not tunneling
my way out of here.

16:07.785 --> 16:11.687
Wow. Can you carve me a set
of women's private parts out of stone?

16:11.789 --> 16:14.019
Sure. Or you could just have sex
with Helen Hunt.

16:16.061 --> 16:20.430
We've only had one conversation, but
I can tell we're gonna be lifelong friends.

16:20.532 --> 16:22.124
And since you're black and I'm white,

16:22.234 --> 16:25.136
that makes it more special
for the audience.

16:31.645 --> 16:32.771
Inspection.

16:40.718 --> 16:42.583
- You Andy Dufresne?
- A little bit. You?

16:43.755 --> 16:45.780
I'm just jiggling your balls.
What can I do for you?

16:45.890 --> 16:48.359
<i>I understand you make
Star Wars figurines.</i>

16:48.594 --> 16:50.494
Oh, Grievous. Wicked!

16:50.596 --> 16:52.359
Well, anyway, I'm a pretty corrupt guy,

16:52.464 --> 16:55.263
so I figured I could sell your figurines
and pocket the cash.

16:55.368 --> 16:57.131
- What do you say?
- I don't know.

16:57.237 --> 17:00.297
Come on. I'll even cripple that guy
who rapes you in the shower.

17:00.407 --> 17:02.034
- But I like that guy.
- Too late.

17:04.845 --> 17:05.937
My legs!

17:06.280 --> 17:09.078
<i>Two things never happened
again after that.</i>

17:09.417 --> 17:11.215
<i>Bogs never walked again,</i>

17:11.319 --> 17:14.015
<i>and Andy's farts never made
a sound again.</i>

17:19.796 --> 17:22.560
<i>Thanks to the Star Wars
figurines Andy carved,</i>

17:22.665 --> 17:25.532
<i>he landed a cushy job
cleaning the warden's office.</i>

17:25.635 --> 17:29.470
Okay, you clean up the warden's office
while I go pop out a pinecone.

17:29.573 --> 17:30.767
Hey, you know what'd be funny?

17:30.874 --> 17:33.741
You should take one of those records
and play it over the PA system.

17:33.844 --> 17:35.676
No, you shouldn't do that,
but it'd be funny.

17:35.780 --> 17:38.010
Okay, I'll be back
in three and a half minutes,

17:38.116 --> 17:41.108
the average length of a song
on any long-playing album.

17:51.344 --> 17:53.175
<i>A few times
I've been around that track</i>

17:53.279 --> 17:55.338
<i>So it's not just gonna happen like that</i>

17:55.448 --> 17:57.678
<i>'Cause I ain't no hollaback girl</i>

17:57.784 --> 18:00.015
<i>I ain't no hollaback girl</i>

18:01.322 --> 18:05.588
<i>To this day, I have no idea
what that woman was singing about.</i>

18:05.693 --> 18:07.958
<i>Like, literally no idea.</i>

18:08.063 --> 18:10.657
<i>I don't know what a hollaback girl is,</i>

18:10.765 --> 18:14.360
<i>but I have to imagine
it's a foul, disease-ridden thing</i>

18:14.469 --> 18:20.170
<i>that wears too much makeup to cover up
the fact that it's a 47-year-old fish dog.</i>

18:20.743 --> 18:23.975
Andy, I think you know
why I've called you in here today.

18:24.081 --> 18:28.415
A prison is an environment which requires
the highest level of discipline.

18:28.518 --> 18:30.952
And that little stunt you pulled today...

18:31.889 --> 18:34.949
That little stunt you pulled today made
a lot of people look very foolish.

18:35.059 --> 18:36.754
Look, Warden, we got it rough in here.

18:36.861 --> 18:38.328
I just thought we could use a little music.

18:38.429 --> 18:41.422
Music is expressly forbidden
inside prison walls.

18:41.533 --> 18:43.330
My God! How can you be so obtuse?

18:43.435 --> 18:46.029
- What did you call me?
- Obtuse. You're being obtuse.

18:46.138 --> 18:47.265
Two months in the hole.

18:47.374 --> 18:50.434
- Or am I being obtuse?
- No, now you're being acute.

18:52.235 --> 18:54.829
<i>That time in the hole
changed old Andy.</i>

18:55.305 --> 18:57.432
I'm getting out of here tonight, Red.

18:57.541 --> 18:59.771
I'm gonna take the poop pipe
to the crap swamp.

18:59.877 --> 19:02.209
Wow. Where are you headed
once you get out?

19:02.312 --> 19:04.838
- Zihuatanejo.
- Sounds fancy.

19:04.949 --> 19:07.008
Well, actually, it's a filthy Mexican village.

19:07.118 --> 19:11.351
Listen, Red, when you get out of here,
I want you to do something for me.

19:11.457 --> 19:14.984
Up in a hayfield in Buxton, Maine,
under an old oak tree,

19:15.094 --> 19:18.086
there's a rock that has
no earthly business being there.

19:18.264 --> 19:21.757
It's black volcanic glass,
has no business being there.

19:21.868 --> 19:25.463
Under that rock is a box
with something I want you to have.

19:25.572 --> 19:27.632
Of course, now I think about it,
I've been in here 25 years.

19:27.742 --> 19:30.643
All these landmarks are based
on possibly outdated observations.

19:30.745 --> 19:32.736
That whole area could be
a Walmart by now.

19:32.847 --> 19:36.181
If it is, pick yourself up some nice
cheap pants, and good life to you.

19:37.953 --> 19:39.386
Inspection.

19:44.227 --> 19:46.457
Dufresne? Dufresne?

19:46.863 --> 19:50.890
Dufresne, you better get your ass out here
before you make me cut this sentence...

19:56.006 --> 19:58.634
- Where is he? Where the hell is Dufresne?
- I don't know, sir.

19:58.742 --> 20:00.404
Hey, we have almost the same voice.

20:00.512 --> 20:03.208
Excuse me, I'm the prison doctor.
I'm here for Andy's check-up.

20:03.315 --> 20:04.976
- Andy Dufresne?
- Yeah, Andy Dufresne.

20:05.083 --> 20:06.914
- We can't find him.
- Well, that's no good.

20:07.018 --> 20:08.611
All right, you two are gonna have to leave.

20:09.188 --> 20:15.458
<i>I want him found now.
Not after breakfast, not after CSI, now.</i>

20:15.762 --> 20:19.220
God, I'm so angry I could just throw
a rock at that poster of David Cassidy.

20:41.635 --> 20:43.899
<i>What the warden
and his boys didn't realize</i>

20:44.004 --> 20:48.601
<i>was that Andy Dufresne had escaped
from Shawshank Prison the night before.</i>

20:59.088 --> 21:03.219
<i>So no one told you
life was gonna be this way</i>

21:06.163 --> 21:07.596
<i>Andy crawled to freedom</i>

21:07.697 --> 21:11.156
<i>through 500 yards of foulness
I can't even imagine.</i>

21:15.106 --> 21:16.232
<i>Andy Dufresne,</i>

21:16.340 --> 21:18.365
<i>the man who crawled
through a river of poop</i>

21:18.476 --> 21:21.173
<i>and came out clean on the other side.</i>

21:23.315 --> 21:26.580
<i>Why he chose enchilada night,
I will never know.</i>

21:28.888 --> 21:32.324
Do you believe in your best judgment
that you have been rehabilitated?

21:32.425 --> 21:33.653
Rehabilitated?

21:33.760 --> 21:35.991
It's just a stupid made-up word

21:36.096 --> 21:41.295
so boys like you can sit behind a desk,
wear a fancy suit, and feel important.

21:41.402 --> 21:44.566
You're a jerk,
and I had sex with your mother last night.

21:44.673 --> 21:49.133
And I swear to God, you let me out of here,
first thing I'm gonna do is kill again.

21:51.948 --> 21:56.112
<i>When I got out of Shawshank,
there was only one thing on my mind.</i>

21:56.219 --> 21:59.747
<i>A promise I made to a friend
that I had to keep.</i>

22:01.592 --> 22:04.720
<i>Walk along the stone wall
until you reach the tree,</i>

22:04.828 --> 22:07.297
<i>and that's where you'll find the rock.</i>

22:21.576 --> 22:26.014
<i>'"Dear Red, if you've come this far,
maybe you're willing to go a little further.</i>

22:26.114 --> 22:29.140
<i>'"You remember the name
of the town in Mexico, right? '"</i>

22:30.085 --> 22:31.052
Shit!

22:36.059 --> 22:39.928
What? Is that him? Is that...
No, no. Beach dog.

22:41.866 --> 22:44.960
Is that Red? Is it... No, no. Not him either.

22:45.069 --> 22:46.195
Where the hell is that jack-off?

22:46.303 --> 22:48.238
There's, like, 1,200 bucks in that box.

22:48.340 --> 22:52.436
Oh, my God. If he ran off with that,
oh, I am gonna be so pissed.

22:52.544 --> 22:54.068
And what am I gonna do,
go to the authorities?

22:54.179 --> 22:55.943
I just broke out of prison. Now what?

22:56.048 --> 22:58.448
I gotta spend the rest of my life
here by myself?

22:58.551 --> 23:01.782
Well, at least I won't have
to be self-conscious about my farting.

23:03.089 --> 23:04.421
Well, that's our show.

23:04.525 --> 23:07.016
Thank you, Stephen King.
We'll see you in court.

23:07.127 --> 23:10.358
Now stay tuned for whatever
Fox is limping to the barn with.

23:10.359 --> 24:11.359
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru